  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Reject ambiguous highest-priority crypto providers",
      "description": "Sorting does not resolve equal priorities: `DefaultCryptoProvider`, `WildFlyElytronProvider`, and `FIPS1402Provider` all return `200`. If multiple full providers are present, selection now depends on service-discovery order instead of rejecting the configuration as before. In particular, the presence of the FIPS provider does not guarantee its selection alongside the default provider.\n\nRetain the lower-priority authz-client fallback, but reject configurations with multiple providers sharing the highest priority unless an explicit selection mechanism resolves them. Add provider-selection tests covering this case.",
      "file_ref": null,
      "category": "security-hygiene",
      "raw_category": null,
      "location": "common/src/main/java/org/keycloak/common/crypto/CryptoIntegration.java:55-57"
    },
    {
      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Enforce ASN.1 sequence boundaries",
      "description": "`readSequence()` reads children from the entire input and accepts a child that exceeds the sequence\u2019s remaining length. For example, `30 04 02 01 01 02 01 01` declares four content bytes but contains two three-byte integers. The decoder consumes both, lets `length` become negative, and returns them successfully; `asn1derToConcatenatedRS()` then accepts the result.\n\nDecode within a bounded sequence-content buffer, reject children exceeding that boundary, and verify complete consumption. Add malformed-length tests so invalid signature encodings cannot be silently normalized.",
      "file_ref": null,
      "category": "correctness",
      "raw_category": null,
      "location": "authz/client/src/main/java/org/keycloak/authorization/client/util/crypto/ASN1Decoder.java:55-62"
    },
    {
      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Exercise the actual curves and verify converted signatures",
      "description": "Every test generates the same provider-default EC curve; the ES384 and ES512 cases change only the digest and output width. They therefore do not exercise full-width P-384/P-521 integers or the long-form sequence length normally needed by P-521 signatures.\n\nThe assertion also compares two outputs of the new converter without checking that the converted DER signature remains valid. Matching conversion errors can pass this round-trip test.\n\nInitialize the generator explicitly with `secp256r1`, `secp384r1`, and `secp521r1` respectively, then verify the converted signature using JCA and the public key. Include deterministic vectors for sign-padding and long-form lengths.",
      "file_ref": null,
      "category": "test-debt",
      "raw_category": null,
      "location": "authz/client/src/test/java/org/keycloak/authorization/client/test/ECDSAAlgorithmTest.java:41-56"
    }
  ],
